Note on the reported line numbers
---------------------------------
Mojo reports the abort location as `endian_error_kind.mojo:19:14` while the
`abort(...)` statement is on source line 20. The `:19` is the source span the
runtime prints (the statement's start), not the physical `abort` line; the log
records the raw runtime output verbatim. This is why the numbers here may differ
from a naive `grep -n abort` (source line 20). No inconsistency — the log is the
captured command output.

`cd akku/prim_endian && task test` stops at the first file
---------------------------------------------------------
The per-library runner (`libraries.sh test`) stops at the first non-zero exit,
so `task test` reports only the first file:

  == _tests/test_prim_endian_endian_error.mojo
  ABORT: ./akku/prim_endian/endian_error.mojo:14:14: MojoAkku: this API is not yet implemented
  task: Failed to run task "test": exit status 1

Note on the scaffold fix
------------------------
The first baseline run failed with a parse error: the stubs called `abort(...)`
without `from std.os import abort`. `task compile` missed it because it emits
`from akku.prim_endian import *` and Mojo resolves `import *` lazily. The
scaffold was corrected (Phase-7 rework, recorded in the Phase-8 commit) by
adding `from std.os import abort` to all 9 API files; the red state above is the
result. This is exactly the defect net_socket fixed in
"phase 7 rework: import abort for instantiated stubs" (commit e8378aa).

